    "question": {
      ":question/id": "de135ab6-432a-57f1-b2d6-0f5028aa982e",
      ":question/problem": "In the year $2007$, there were approximately $9280$ crimes in a particular city. The police department then promised a $10.6\\%$ annual *decrease* in crime, continuously compounded. According to this model, how many crimes occurred in $2016$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=9280$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-10.6/100=-0.106$. The elapsed time is $t=2016-2007=9$ years.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 9280e^{(-0.106)(9)} \\\\\n&= 9280e^{-0.954} \\\\\n&= 9280(0.3851971\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 3575\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to this model, approximately $3575$ crimes occurred in $2016$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
