    "question": {
      ":question/id": "58af2321-96ba-56ee-ab5b-86b20014de68",
      ":question/problem": "In medieval times, there were $7990$ people living in a city struck by a plague. If the disease resulted in a daily *decrease* in the population at a continuously compounded rate of $7.9\\%$, what was the city's population after $2$ weeks? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The continuously compounded growth equation is $P=P_0e^{rt}$. The initial amount is $P_0=7990$. Since the amount decreases, the signed decimal rate is $r=-7.9/100=-0.079$. The rate is daily, so convert the duration to days: $t=2\\times 7=14$ days.\n\nSubstitute these values and round only the final amount:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n&= 7990e^{(-0.079)(14)} \\\\\n&= 7990e^{-1.106} \\\\\n&= 7990(0.3308798\\ldots) \\\\\n&\\approx 2644\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAfter $2$ weeks, the population was approximately $2644$ people.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/requires-calculator": true,
